WEBVTT

00:07:25.831 --> 00:07:30.060
that improves access to health care,
education, civil rights.

00:07:30.839 --> 00:07:33.916
And what we've seen in our research
in the United States Congress

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.108
is that women sponsor more legislation

00:07:36.132 --> 00:07:37.927
and they cosponsor more legislation.

00:07:37.951 --> 00:07:41.705
So all the evidence is that when women
actually have the chance to serve,

00:07:41.729 --> 00:07:44.752
they make a huge difference
and they get the job done.

00:07:45.155 --> 00:07:49.243
So how would it look in the United States
if different people were making decisions?

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:53.768
Well, I firmly believe
if half of Congress could get pregnant,

00:07:53.792 --> 00:07:56.220
we would finally quit fighting
about birth control

00:07:56.244 --> 00:07:57.429
and Planned Parenthood.

00:07:57.453 --> 00:07:58.599
(Applause and cheers)

00:07:58.623 --> 00:07:59.774
That would be over.

00:07:59.798 --> 00:08:04.870
(Applause)